#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0898 expect=violation domain=ADLB
#note "Fix #358 (PLAN-match-datasets-split-union.md): the parent LB ships SPLIT (LBCH/LBHE, DOMAIN=LB, no standalone LB). The expansion binds &DOM& to LB (the prefix of LBSEQ); the Match_Datasets join and the Check-side dotted var_exists both resolve LB to the member UNION, so row 1 (LBSEQ=1, in LBCH) and row 2 (LBSEQ=9, in LBHE) match while row 3 (LBSEQ=7) matches NO member and fires. Before the union this rule was a silent no-op on split submissions: var_exists(`LB.LBSEQ`) resolved nothing and short-circuited to false."
#library standard=adamig version=1-2
#library standard-domains AE CM MH DM LB VS
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 LBSEQ=7
dataset ADLB
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col LBSEQ   type=Char
col PARAM   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALT
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 9 | HGB
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 7 | PH
---

dataset LBCH label="Laboratory Test Results (Chemistry)"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col LBSEQ   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1
---

dataset LBHE label="Laboratory Test Results (Hematology)"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col LBSEQ   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 9
---
